<title>USA: State of emergency for three Maine counties.</title>
<headline>State of emergency for three Maine counties.</headline>
<dateline>AUGUSTA, Maine 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine Governor Angus King on Monday declared a state of emergency for three rain-soaked counties in the southern part of the state.</p>
<p>King declared a state of emergency for York, Cumberland and Oxford counties where record breaking rain has fallen in the last 24-hours and roads and highways are flooded.</p>
<p>--Boston bureau, 617-367-4106</p>
</text>
